  "_comment": "Disease states for graph matching (Documentation/design/graph-normalization.md#ranking). They apply to a paper on one of the patient's cancers; `prostate` states only to a prostate cancer paper of a prostate cancer patient. A paper is about a state when its title matches `title` (case-insensitive, JavaScript) or one of `mesh` is a major topic. A patient is in a state when an active statement has one of `concepts`, or an entity name matches `names` (German and English, after normalizeName). Which states contradict each other is in stages.ts. `treatment` and `diagnosis` are the MeSH IDs that, as a major topic, make a prostate cancer paper one about treating or about finding the disease; for other diseases the qualifiers of the patient's diagnosis and the kind of a procedure decide (stages.ts). A paper on treatment ranks lower while the patient is still being diagnosed, one only on diagnosis ranks a little lower once his treatment has begun. `alternatives` are prostate cancer treatment options (brachytherapy, radiosurgery, HIFU, hypofractionation, orchiectomy and the like): after his treatment began, a paper with one of them as a major topic that the patient did not get ranks a little lower.",
